2026-11-20  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	MODULE_<NAME> is a boolean: ON (default) or OFF, never AUTO, so a
	module is not chosen by which libraries are installed.

	* CMakeLists.txt: option(MODULE_<NAME> ... ON); a value other than a
	boolean (the old AUTO) stops the configure.
	* cmake/Deps.cmake: synced; dep_module_mode() rejects AUTO, DEPS_MISSING
	defaults to FAIL (DISABLE is an explicit opt-in).
	* cmake/{FindQuickJS,BuildQuickJS,QuickJSModule}.cmake: synced.

	Fix the failing binding tests (all 22 ctest tests pass).

	* quickjs-stk.cpp (js_stkinstrmnt_constructor): instruments carry their
	own Symbol.toStringTag ([object Clarinet]), like generators and filters.
	* quickjs-labsound.cpp (js_stereopanner_constructor): pan starts at 0.
	* tests/bindings/stk-test.js: setChannel takes an StkFrames, rawwave
	path set from third_party/stk/rawwaves, filter setters and the
	Generator/Filter/Effect members no longer assumed.
	* tests/bindings/labsound-test.js: float32 tolerance, no
	numberOfChannels, buffer compared by length and sampleRate.
	* tests/bindings/portaudio-test.js: getters that PaStream really has.

2026-11-18  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	Project-tree cleanup: every bound library is now a Deps.cmake
	dependency, installed or vendored, chosen per library.

	* cmake/Deps.cmake (new): synced from the quickjs-native-bindings
	skill (its MANIFEST scope now lists qjs-sound).
	* cmake/deps/SoundLibs.cmake (new): registers portaudio, portmidi,
	sndfile, samplerate, soundtouch, rubberband, fftw3, aubio, stk and
	labsound with dep_declare(). BUILD_<LIB> is AUTO (installed, else
	vendored), ON (always vendored) or OFF (installed only); the old
	two-state BUILD_<LIB> options are the ON/OFF cases. An installed
	copy is still pinned with <LIB>_PREFIX, <LIB>_INCLUDE_DIR and
	<LIB>_LIBRARY_DIR. aubio keeps its "installed copy needs FFTW3"
	probe and depends on fftw3; stk is now also found as an installed
	library (it was always built before).
	* cmake/deps/Build{LabSound,Stk}.cmake (new): the LabSound (patched in
	place) and stk ExternalProjects, moved out of CMakeLists.txt.
	* cmake/deps/{BuildAubio,BuildFFTW3,BuildPortAudio,BuildPortMIDI,
	BuildRubberBand,BuildSampleRate,BuildSndFile,BuildSoundTouch,
	VendoredLibrary}.cmake: moved from cmake/; the Find<Lib>.cmake
	files are gone (their lookup is SoundLibs.cmake's generic find).
	* CMakeLists.txt: MODULE_<NAME> (AUTO, ON, OFF) replaces USE_<NAME>,
	which still switches a module off; a module whose library is neither
	installed nor built is skipped with a warning (DEPS_MISSING=FAIL
	stops instead); a table of where each library came from is printed
	when the configure ends. The vendored-library tests (LabSound,
	aubio) are wired only when that library was built, since only the
	vendored copy carries the patches.
	* CLAUDE.md: build options and the patch wiring rules describe the
	new layout.
	* not synced: FindQuickJS.cmake, BuildQuickJS.cmake and
	QuickJSModule.cmake. The skill's canonical copies are older than
	this project's (they lack the CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING guard and
	hide_static_symbols), so apply would undo fixes.
	* web/ (new, proof of concept, not published): STK and SndObj DSP
	built to one standalone wasm (qjs-sound-web.wasm, 162 KB, em++ 6.0.10)
	and wrapped in an AudioWorkletProcessor (worklet.js), with a demo page
	(index.html: oscillator -> worklet -> gain -> destination). One wasm
	call per 128-frame block: STK BiQuad (filter), STK Plucked
	(instrument), SndObj Reson (filter). web/test.mjs drives the processor
	under node (resonance passes its frequency, a plucked string decays);
	2-11 us per block against a 2902 us budget at 44.1 kHz. Not yet run
	in a browser. Compiles for wasm: 80 of 90 STK sources (all but the
	Inet/Tcp/Udp/Socket/Thread/Mutex/RtWv* I/O files; RtAudio.cpp and
	RtMidi.cpp only compile, they are device I/O and are left out) and 94
	of 113 SndObj sources (not: the FFT/phase-vocoder family, AdSyn,
	ReSyn, SinAnal, SinSyn, Convol, IFAdd, IFGram, PVA/PVS/PVRead,
	PVTable, ImpulseTable, SndPVOCEX, SndRTThread, SndSinIO; they need
	rfftw, which the tree does not ship). emsdk's cache dir is read-only
	here, so build with EM_CACHE=<writable dir>.

2026-11-17  Roman Senn  <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>

	Fix the bugs listed in BUGS; every fixed bug got a regression test.

	* quickjs-portaudio.c (js_pastream_format_kind, METHOD_READ,
	METHOD_WRITE): pastream-buffer-format-not-validated fixed. read()
	and write() now reject a TypedArray whose element kind does not
	match the stream's negotiated sampleFormat, throwing a TypeError
	instead of silently reinterpreting every sample's bytes as the
	wrong type.
	* js-typedarray.c, js-typedarray.h: add js_typedarray_kind_from_bpe,
	a helper used by the pastream format check to map a bytes-per-element
	value back to the TypedArrayKind the read/write buffer arguments are
	validated against.
	* quickjs-stk.cpp: stk-tostringtag-array-out-of-enum-order fixed.
	The generator and effect ctor_def tables are indexed by magic and
	must follow the INSTANCE enum order; Blit, BlitSaw, BlitSquare and
	PRCRev, PitShift were listed in the wrong order, so every instance
	reported the previous entry's toStringTag. Table order now matches
	the enums.
	* cmake/BuildQuickJS.cmake: build-quickjs-forwards-cmake-system-name
	fixed. CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, CMAKE_SYSROOT and the toolchain file are
	now forwarded to the nested quickjs configure only when this project
	is itself cross-compiling (CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING), so on a native
	build (e.g. Termux) CMake no longer sets CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING=TRUE
	and the qjsc "No such file or directory" failure is avoided.
	* CMakeLists.txt (LabSound, stk ExternalProject_Add):
	externalproject-cmp0225-labsound-stk fixed. Both external projects
	now pass CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX so CMake 4.5 no longer warns about
	policy CMP0225, and there is now only one CMP0225-gated warning.
	* cmake/VendoredLibrary.cmake (vendored_build_static_subdirectory):
	PATCH now takes several patch files, applied in order, each verified
	reversible; the build-tree copy is stamped on the concatenated
	content hashes of all patches so any edit rebuilds it. Lets a
	vendored library's own patch and a follow-up bug fix (the aubio
	confidence patch) be wired together without editing the submodule.
	* cmake/BuildAubio.cmake: wire patches/aubio-pitch-confidence-reads-
	zero.patch in alongside the existing static-lib patch, so the aubio
	confidence fix ships in the vendored build.
	* patches/aubio-pitch-confidence-reads-zero.patch (new):
	aubio-pitch-confidence-reads-zero fixed in the library. The yinfft
	method set peak_pos only in its short-period branch; for tau >
	short_period (a 440 Hz sine at 44100 Hz) it stayed 0 and confidence
	read 1 - yinfft->data[0] == 0. peak_pos is now set to tau there.
	* tests/vendor/aubio-pitch-confidence-reads-zero.cpp (new), CMakeLists.txt:
	C++ regression test linked straight against the vendored aubio; wired
	with add_test only when BUILD_AUBIO is ON (the system copy is unpatched).
	* tests/bindings/*.js: use std.exit() instead of the undefined
	process.exit(); drop a reassignment of a const in the getters test.
	* CLAUDE.md: document the vendored-library patch and test
	conventions (patch file format, patches/ vs cmake/patches/, C++
	regression tests in tests/vendor/ for library bugs and JS tests in
	tests/bindings/ for binding bugs, ctest wiring).
	* tests/bindings/portaudio-pastream-buffer-format.js (new):
	regression test for pastream-buffer-format-not-validated; a
	paFloat32 stream rejects a Float64Array/Int16Array read/write with
	a TypeError while an ArrayBuffer (no element kind) is still
	accepted. Skips the device-dependent success path in a
	device-less sandbox.
	* tests/bindings/stk-tostringtag-order.js (new): regression test
	for stk-tostringtag-array-out-of-enum-order; every generator and
	effect reports its own toStringTag.
	* CMakeLists.txt: wire both new binding tests into ctest under the
	existing QJSM guard.
	* test-labsound.cpp, test-labsound.hpp: removed. The unwired C++
	LabSound smoke test is superseded by the ctest-wired regression
	tests in tests/vendor/ and tests/bindings/.

	Later the same day:
	* cmake/Checks.cmake (check_cflag): check-cflag-result-cached-under-
	fixed-name fixed. The probe result was cached under the fixed name
	RESULT, so every flag after the first got the first answer; each
	flag now has its own cache variable (CHECK_CFLAG_<flag>).
	* tests/cmake/check-cflag-result-cached/CMakeLists.txt (new),
	CMakeLists.txt: ctest regression test probing a supported and a
	bogus flag in one configure.
	* quickjs-labsound.cpp (read_float_array, js_audiocontext_create_node):
	labsound-waveshapernode-offline-silent fixed, and it was a binding
	bug, not an engine bug. read_float_array returned -1 on success
	(copy_array returns 0 on success), so every curve passed from JS was
	dropped and the shaper had an empty curve, which the engine renders
	as silence; the same inversion made AudioBuffer.copyToChannel(array)
	throw. createWaveShaper({ curve }) also never forwarded its options
	object to the constructor; it does now.
	* tests/bindings/labsound-waveshapernode-offline-silent.js (new),
	CMakeLists.txt: ctest regression test for all three ways to set a
	curve and for copyToChannel.

	LabSound engine fixes, applied to the submodule tree at build time
	by cmake/ApplyPatches.cmake (idempotent PATCH_COMMAND of the LabSound
	ExternalProject); each has a C++ test in tests/vendor/ linked
	against the patched library:
	* patches/labsound-disconnect-deferred-wipes-later-connect.patch:
	a Connect touching a node with a pending FinishDisconnect is requeued
	behind it, so disconnect() followed by connect() keeps the new edge.
	* patches/labsound-scheduler-epoch-inconsistent-start-stop.patch:
	start/stop times are absolute context time (no epoch term).
	quickjs-labsound.cpp: engine_when no longer subtracts the epoch.
	* patches/labsound-compressor-channel-assert.patch:
	AudioNodeOutput::setNumberOfChannels drops a stale in-place bus, so
	a mono source into a stereo destination no longer trips the
	compressor's channel assertion.
	* patches/labsound-stopped-source-stuck-stopping.patch:
	disconnectAll() completes the stop (UNSCHEDULED, onEnded) of a source
	cut while STOPPING; confirmed by the test before the fix.
	* labsound-functionnode-offline-silent: not reproducible, a
	FunctionNode renders offline; tests/vendor/ keeps a guard test.
	* pastream-reopen-after-close-segfault: not reproducible any more
	(open, close, open exits cleanly); tests/bindings/ keeps a test.
	* console-error-warn-undefined-qjsm: the installed qjsm has
	console.error and console.warn; nothing to fix in this project.
	* CMakeLists.txt: the LabSound test targets depend on the LabSound
	external project so they relink after a library rebuild.
